  "plot": "Cord Jefferson's hilarious directorial debut confronts our culture's obsession with reducing people to outrageous stereotypes. Jeffrey Wright stars as Monk, a frustrated novelist who's fed up with the establishment profiting from \"Black\" entertainment that relies on tired and offensive tropes. To prove his point, Monk uses a pen name to write his own outlandish \"Black\" book--that propels him into the heart of hypocrisy and the madness he claims to disdain.",
